n- For each line, row must be distinct from its column 1 row.\n- Sum must be distinct from its column 1 sum.\n\nLet's list possible assignments per line:\n\n- L1 (row1=1, sum2): can assign (2,2) row2, sum4 (distinct from sum2). Can assign (2,3) row3, sum5 (distinct). Cannot assign (2,1) row1 conflict.\n\n- L2 (row2=2, sum3): can assign (2,1) row1, sum3 conflict with sum3 (duplicate). So cannot assign (2,1). Can assign (2,2) row2 conflict. Can assign (2,3) row3, sum5 distinct. So L2 can only assign (2,3).\n\n- L3 (row3=3, sum4): can assign (2,1) row1, sum3 distinct from sum4. Can assign (2,2) row2, sum4 conflict with sum4. Can assign (2,3) row3 conflict. So L3 can only assign (2,1).\n\n- L4 (row4=4, sum5): can assign (2,1) row1, sum3 distinct from sum5. Can assign (2,2) row2, sum4 distinct. Can assign (2,3) row3, sum5 conflict. So L4 can assign (2,1) or (2,2).\n\nNow we need to assign each of (2,1),(2,2),(2,3) to distinct lines. Let's try:\n\n- L2 must get (2,3) (only option). So assign (2,3) to L2.\n\n- L3 must get (2,1) (only option). So assign (2,1) to L3.\n\n- L1 and L4 need to assign (2,2) to one of them. L1 can take (2,2). L4 can also take (2,2). But we need to assign (2,2) to exactly one line, and the other line gets no column 2 point.\n\nThus we have two possibilities:\n\nOption A: L1 gets (2,2), L4 gets none.\n\nOption B: L4 gets (2,2), L1 gets none.\n\nLet's examine each.\n\nOption A: L1: (2,2) sum=4, row2. L1's sums: (1,1) sum=2, (2,2) sum=4. Row used: 1,2. L4: no column 2 point, only (1,4) sum=5, row4.\n\nOption B: L1: no column 2 point, only (1,1). L4: (2,2) sum=4, row2.\n\nNow we need to assign column 3 points (3,1) sum=4, (3,2) sum=5.\n\nWe need to assign each to a line that does not have row conflict and sum conflict.\n\nLet's compute current rows and sums per line for each option.\n\nOption A:\n\n- L1: rows {1,2}, sums {2,4}\n- L2: rows {2,3}, sums {3,5}\n- L3: rows {3,1}, sums {4,3} (since (2,1) sum=3)\n- L4: rows {4}, sums {5}\n\nOption B:\n\n- L1: